Error: Jet.UseWhileWriteActive: `k` is changed by a stored lambda that holds its own copy, so it can't be used here
  --> Tests/UI/Closures/stored_closure_capture_write.jet:9:11
    |
  9 |     print(k)
    |           ^
 Why: A stored lambda owns its captures: its writes land on its copy of `k` and never reach `k` itself
 Fix: Call the lambda only where it is bound so it borrows `k`, or keep the value in a `Shared` or `Cell` the lambda and this code both reach
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.UseWhileWriteActive

